---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream attribution
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is a fork of https://github.com/nloui/paperless-mcp, and parts of
this tree are still derived from that work (most visibly src/api/PaperlessAPI.ts
and the document, tag, correspondent and document-type tool modules).

That repository ships no LICENSE file. Its package.json declares
`"license": "ISC"` and `"author": "Nick Loui"` — from its first commit
(2024-12-27) through today — and the published npm package
`@nloui/paperless-mcp@1.0.0` carries the same declaration and likewise contains
no license text. The ISC terms are therefore reproduced below as they read in
the canonical ISC text, with the copyright line reconstructed from that
`author` field and from the year range of the upstream commits, because
upstream never published a copyright notice of its own. Upstream also has
contributors other than Nick Loui, who retain copyright in their own
contributions; "and the paperless-mcp contributors" above is meant to cover
them.

    ISC License

    Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Nick Loui and the paperless-mcp contributors

    Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
    purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
    copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.

    THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES
    WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR
    ANY SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES
    WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN
    ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF
    OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.

ISC and MIT are both permissive licenses whose only substantive condition is
that the copyright and permission notices travel with the software;
redistributing ISC-licensed code as part of an MIT-licensed work, with the
upstream notice preserved, is common practice. That is what this file does.
If upstream later publishes a LICENSE file, this section should be updated to
match whatever notice it contains.
